## Partially enforced (25 requirements)

The host enforces part of each requirement below. The **Residual** column is
what the organization still owes.

| Requirement | Title | Residual organizational obligation |
|---|---|---|
| 03.01.01 | Account Management | Statements a-d, f.3-f.5, g, h are organizational: defining allowed account types, authorizing users, specifying role membership, notifying account managers, and the behavioural logout policy. Record these in the SSP. |
| 03.01.03 | Information Flow Enforcement | Enterprise flow enforcement between enclaves (guards, proxies, CDS) is an architecture concern outside a single host. |
| 03.01.04 | Separation of Duties | Identifying which duties require separation, and assigning people to those roles, is organizational. |
| 03.01.18 | Access Control for Mobile Devices | Usage restrictions and connection authorization for other mobile devices (statements a, b) are organizational and enforced by MDM, not by this host. |
| 03.01.20 | Use of External Systems | Authorizing external systems and retaining connection agreements (statements a-c) is organizational. |
| 03.03.05 | Audit Record Review, Analysis, and Reporting | A human reviewing the output and reporting findings (statements a, b) is organizational. Forwarding requires a collector address to be set. |
| 03.04.01 | Baseline Configuration | Reviewing and updating the baseline at the ODP frequency (statement b) is a process; the manifest and AIDE database are the artifacts it consumes. |
| 03.04.11 | Information Location | Identifying all CUI across the enterprise is a data-governance activity. |
| 03.05.02 | Device Identification and Authentication | Network-level device authentication (802.1X, MAC allow-listing) is an infrastructure control. |
| 03.05.03 | Multi-Factor Authentication | Issuing and binding the second factor (PIV/CAC credentials, or an OTP provider) requires enterprise identity infrastructure. Enable `mfa_enforce_pubkey` once operators hold keys, or the host will lock out. |
| 03.06.02 | Incident Monitoring, Reporting, and Response Assistance | Tracking, documenting, and reporting incidents, and providing a support resource, are organizational. |
| 03.07.04 | Maintenance Tools | Approving tools and handling equipment removal (statements a, c) are organizational. |
| 03.08.03 | Media Sanitization | Performing and documenting sanitization prior to disposal is a process. |
| 03.08.09 | System Backup - Cryptographic Protection | Off-host backup storage, rotation, and restoration testing are handled by the enterprise backup service. |
| 03.09.02 | Personnel Termination and Transfer | Triggering offboarding on an HR event, and retrieving physical property, are organizational. |
| 03.10.07 | Physical Access Control | Entry/exit enforcement, visitor escorting, key control, and output device control are facility controls. |
| 03.12.01 | Security Assessment | Assessing the environment of operation, and the independence of the assessor, are organizational. |
| 03.12.02 | Plan of Action and Milestones | Assigning owners, remediation dates, and resources is a management activity. |
| 03.12.03 | Continuous Monitoring | Defining the organizational monitoring strategy is governance. |
| 03.13.10 | Cryptographic Key Establishment and Management | Enterprise key lifecycle (escrow, rotation schedule, destruction records) is a KMS function. |
| 03.13.13 | Mobile Code | Defining acceptable mobile code (statement a) is policy. |
| 03.14.03 | Security Alerts, Advisories, and Directives | Subscribing to and disseminating advisories organization-wide is a process. |
| 03.14.08 | Information Management and Retention | Retention of CUI content itself is governed by records-management policy. |
| 03.15.02 | System Security Plan | Threat description, role assignment, and approval are authored by the system owner. |
| 03.17.03 | Supply Chain Requirements and Processes | Supplier assessment and contractual flow-down are procurement processes. |

## How to use this

1. For each row, identify the policy, procedure, or physical control that
   satisfies it, and reference it in the System Security Plan (03.15.02).
2. Where no control exists yet, open a POA&M item (03.12.02).
3. Review at the frequency your organization sets for 03.12.01.
